// Tailnet access policy for tower's Headscale (HuJSON: comments and trailing
// commas are allowed).
//
// This is deliberately equivalent to having no policy at all: with no "acls"
// or "grants" section, Headscale lets every node reach every other node on
// every port. It is committed so that tightening access is a reviewed change
// to this file rather than an edit on the server, and so CI can check it with
// `headscale policy check` on every pull request.
//
// A deploy that changes this file restarts headscale, which reloads it.
//
// To restrict access, add grants. Once any "grants" (or "acls") key exists,
// everything not granted is denied — an empty "grants": [] blocks all traffic.
// Example: members may only reach each other over SSH and SMB:
//
//   "grants": [
//     { "src": ["autogroup:member"], "dst": ["autogroup:member"], "ip": ["tcp:22", "tcp:445"] },
//   ],
//
// Syntax: https://tailscale.com/docs/features/access-control/grants
{}
